</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Petersen</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name> (<year>2008</year>) <article-title>Malaria chemoprophylaxis: strategies for risk groups</article-title>. <source>Clin Microbiol Rev</source><volume>21</volume>: <fpage>466</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>472</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18625682</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0056863-vanRijckevorsel1"><label>8</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>van Rijckevorsel</surname><given-names>GG</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Sonder</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Geskus</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Wetsteyn</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Ligthelm</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name>, <etal>et al</etal> (<year>2010</year>) <article-title>Declining incidence of imported malaria in the Netherlands, 2000&#x02013;2007</article-title>. <source>Malar J 9</source><volume>300</volume><fpage>300</fpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0056863-Gyorkos1"><label>9</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Gyorkos</surname><given-names>TW</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Svenson</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Maclean</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Mohamed</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Remondin</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name>, <etal>et al</etal> (<year>1995</year>) <article-title>Compliance with antimalarial chemoprophylaxis and the subsequent development of malaria: a matched case-control study</article-title>. <source>Am J Trop Med Hyg</source><volume>53</volume>: <fpage>511</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>517</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7485709</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0056863-Kain1"><label>10</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Kain</surname><gi